# SteadyDose environment configuration (example).
# These are only needed when you want cloud sync (auth + multi-device).
# Stages 0–2 / 6 / 7 run fully offline with no env required.
#
# For LOCAL dev you don't fill this in by hand: run `supabase start`, then copy
# the printed "API URL" and "anon key" into .env.local (or run `pnpm local:env`).
# For a real deploy, read them from your Supabase project's API settings.
# The anon key is publishable (RLS protects data); NEVER ship the service-role key.
# Only this example file is tracked — never commit .env.local.

# Supabase (cloud sync)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Background Web Push (Stage 6 follow-up). OPTIONAL: with this empty the app uses
# in-app catch-up and notifications that only fire while it is open. To enable
# server-sent push that arrives when the app is CLOSED, generate a VAPID keypair
# (e.g. `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`) and:
#   - put the PUBLIC key here (it ships to the client; not a secret), and
#   - set the PRIVATE key + VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY/VAPID_SUBJECT as send-push Edge
#     Function secrets via `supabase secrets set …`.
# NEVER commit the private key. See supabase/functions/send-push and migration 0005.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=

# Oura Ring health data (Stage 13). OPTIONAL and MOCK-BY-DEFAULT: with nothing set
# the app uses deterministic offline sample data. Real OAuth/token auth is NOT
# wired yet — setting `live` only takes effect once a token is supplied here (the
# auth seam). NEVER commit a real token; .env.local is untracked.
# VITE_OURA_MODE=live
# VITE_OURA_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# VITE_OURA_API_BASE=https://api.ouraring.com
